- name: note_0_0
  id: note
  parameters:
    alias: ''
    comment: ''
    note: Transmitter Side Flow
  states:
    bus_sink: false
    bus_source: false
    bus_structure: null
    coordinate: [72, 328.0]
    rotation: 0
    state: enabled
- name: note_2
  id: note
  parameters:
    alias: ''
    comment: "USAGE NOTES FOR FILE, IMAGE, AND VIDEO TRANSFER\nTo send a TXT file\
      \ or an image, use the File Source and File Sink blocks, and disable the UDP\
      \ blocks.\nTo send video, use the UDP blocks, and disable the File Source and\
      \ File Sink blocks.\nThis is the same for simulation as well.\nFor the transmitter\
      \ side, use only the upper side of the flowgraph, up to the USRP Sink block,\
      \ and disable the bottom side of the flowgraph.\nFor the receiver side, do the\
      \ opposite.\nThrottle, Tag Gate, Virtual Sink (stream ID: \"transmit\")\_, and\
      \ Virtual Source(stream ID: \"transmit\") blocks are only for simulation.\n\
      Keep them disabled during real tests with USRP.\nWhen doing simulation only,\
      \ enable both the transmitter and receiver sides.\nEnable Throttle, Tag Gate,\
      \ and the Virtual Sink and Virtual Source blocks that have the stream ID: \"\
      transmit\".\nDisable the UHD blocks during simulation.\nFor video transfer,\
      \ if you are on the receiver side, run the RX Python file from the Linux terminal\
      \ and from its original directory, not randomly from another location.\nThen\
      \ run the receiver-side flowgraph.\nIf you are on the transmitter side, run\
      \ the flowgraph first.\nThen run the TX Python file from the terminal and from\
      \ the original directory of the TX file.\nMake sure your computer camera is\
      \ open and not disabled by the camera key on the keyboard.\nThe UHD block addresses\
      \ on both the receiver and transmitter sides must be selected according to the\
      \ SDR devices being used.\n2-channel USRP X310 address: \"addr=192.168.10.2\"\
      \n1-channel USRP Ettus X310 address: \"addr=192.168.10.3\""
    note: USAGE NOTES
  states:
    bus_sink: false
    bus_source: false
    bus_structure: null
    coordinate: [1624, 32.0]
    rotation: 0
    state: enabled
- name: note_2_0
  id: note
  parameters:
    alias: ''
    comment: 'GENERAL OVERVIEW

      This is an SDR system that sends digital DATA / VIDEO using BPSK.

      Data -> bits -> BPSK signal -> antenna (869.525 MHz) -> bits again -> data.

      UPPER half = TRANSMITTER, LOWER half = RECEIVER.

      samp_rate = 1.75 MHz, sps = 4, meaning 4 samples per symbol, modulation = BPSK.'
    note: GENERAL OVERVIEW
  states:
    bus_sink: false
    bus_source: false
    bus_structure: null
    coordinate: [2024, 688.0]
    rotation: 0
    state: enabled
- name: note_3
  id: note
  parameters:
    alias: ''
    comment: 'CONTROL KNOBS (shown in tabs when the program starts)

      tx_baseband_gain : internal amplitude of the transmitted signal

      Transmit Gain    : radio transmit power

      Receive Gain     : radio receive gain

      Time: BW         : speed of the symbol timing lock in the receiver

      Phase: Bandwidth : speed of the phase / carrier correction in the receiver,
      Costas loop'
    note: CONTROL KNOBS
  states:
    bus_sink: false
    bus_source: false
    bus_structure: null
    coordinate: [2024, 880.0]
    rotation: 0
    state: enabled
- name: note_4
  id: note
  parameters:
    alias: ''
    comment: "TRANSMITTER PATH (upper row, left to right)\n\n1. UDP/File Source: brings\
      \ the bytes to be transmitted.\n2. Stream to Tagged Stream: divides the bytes\
      \ into packets (payload_size = 1000).\n3. CRC32: adds an error-checking code\
      \ to the packet.\n4. Protocol Formatter + Tagged Stream Mux: adds the header,\
      \ access code + length,\n   and combines the header + data into one packet.\n\
      5. Constellation Modulator (BPSK): converts the bits into a signal.\n6. x tx_baseband_gain\
      \ -> USRP Sink: transmits it from the antenna.\n   Time Sink shows the transmitted\
      \ samples."
    note: TRANSMITTER PATH (upper row, left to right)
  states:
    bus_sink: false
    bus_source: false
    bus_structure: null
    coordinate: [2032, 1072.0]
    rotation: 0
    state: enabled
- name: note_5
  id: note
  parameters:
    alias: ''
    comment: 'RECEIVER PATH (bottom row, left to right)


      1. USRP Source: receives the signal from the antenna.

      2. RRC Filter: matched filter that corresponds to the shaping used in the transmitter,
      reducing noise.

      3. Symbol Sync: samples at the correct instant, meaning symbol timing.

      4. Costas Loop: corrects phase / frequency offset, visible on the Constellation
      display.

      5. Constellation Decoder + Diff Decoder: converts the signal back into bits.

      6. Correlate Access Code: finds the start of the packet. Repack Bits: collects
      bits into bytes.

      7. CRC32 (check): discards corrupted packets. UDP/File Sink: outputs the recovered
      data.'
    note: RECEIVER PATH (bottom row, left to right)
  states:
    bus_sink: false
    bus_source: false
    bus_structure: null
    coordinate: [2032, 1376.0]
    rotation: 0
    state: enabled
